+## Setup
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+- Node.js 18 or newer
+- npm
+- Python 3 (only needed for `npm run seed`)
+- Docker (optional, for running the container)
+
+### Install and configure
+
+```sh
+npm ci
+cp .env.example .env
+```
+
+Edit `.env` and set real values for `SESSION_SECRET` and `ADMIN_TOKEN`. Both default to empty if unset, and the `change-me` placeholders are not safe to use.
+
+| Variable | Default | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `PORT` | `3000` | Port the server listens on |
+| `DATABASE_URL` | `sqlite:./data/dev.db` | Database connection string |
+| `SESSION_SECRET` | _(empty)_ | Secret used for session auth |
+| `ADMIN_TOKEN` | _(empty)_ | Token for the admin endpoints |
+| `STAGING_API_URL` | `https://staging.notes.internal` | Staging API base URL |
+
+### Run
+
+```sh
+npm start        # start the server
+npm run dev      # start with auto-reload on file changes
+```
+
+The server listens on `http://localhost:3000` by default.
+
+### Seed sample data (optional)
+
+```sh
+npm run seed
+```
+
+This writes 25 sample notes to `data/seed.json`, which is git-ignored.
+
+### Tests
+
+```sh
+npm test
+```
+
+### Docker
+
+```sh
+docker build -t notes-api .
+docker run --env-file .env -p 3000:3000 notes-api
+```
+
 ## Development
 
-Copy `.env.example` to `.env`, then run `npm start`.
+Use `npm run dev` for local development. See Setup above for configuration.
